{"id": "swebq0113", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 3.06, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2988, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "University of Oregon", "query": "what is the oregon ducks 2012 football schedule?", "transcript": "What is the Oregon Ducks twenty twelve football schedule?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The **2012 Oregon Ducks football schedule** was as follows. They started with games against Arkansas State, Fresno State, Tennessee Tech, and Arizona at home, winning each by significant margins. Their first road game was against Washington State in Seattle, which they also won. The team then returned home for a matchup against Washington before heading to Tempe to play Arizona State. After another strong performance at home against Colorado, the season continued with wins over USC in Los Angeles, California, and Stanford at Berkeley. Oregon faced their only loss of the regular season in an overtime game against Stanford on their home turf. The final home game was against Oregon State. The year concluded with a Fiesta Bowl victory over Kansas State in Glendale, Arizona. Overall, the Ducks finished the 2012 season with a **12–1 record**.", "expert_answer": "The **2012 Oregon Ducks football schedule** was:\n\n| Date | Opponent | Location | Result |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| Sept. 1 | Arkansas State | Eugene, OR | W 57–34 |\n| Sept. 8 | Fresno State | Eugene, OR | W 42–25 |\n| Sept. 15 | Tennessee Tech | Eugene, OR | W 63–14 |\n| Sept. 22 | Arizona | Eugene, OR | W 49–0 |\n| Sept. 29 | Washington State | Seattle, WA | W 51–26 |\n| Oct. 6 | Washington | Eugene, OR | W 52–21 |\n| Oct. 18 | Arizona State | Tempe, AZ | W 43–21 |\n| Oct. 27 | Colorado | Eugene, OR | W 70–14 |\n| Nov. 3 | USC | Los Angeles, CA | W 62–51 |\n| Nov. 10 | California | Berkeley, CA | W 59–17 |\n| Nov. 17 | Stanford | Eugene, OR | L 17–14 OT |\n| Nov. 24 | Oregon State | Corvallis, OR | W 48–24 |\n| Jan. 3, 2013 | Kansas State — Fiesta Bowl | Glendale, AZ | W 35–17 |\n\nOregon finished the 2012 season **12–1**.", "expert_latency_s": 11.43, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 4210}
{"id": "swebq0116", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.51, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3472, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "william averell harriman appointed by john fitzgerald kennedy", "query": "who did john kennedy have affairs with?", "transcript": "Who did John Kennedy have affairs with?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "John F. Kennedy is reported to have had affairs or relationships with several women, though some claims are disputed. Notable names include Marilyn Monroe, Judith Campbell Exner, Mimi Alford, Mary Pinchot Meyer, Gunilla von Post, Inga Arvad, Pamela Turnure, and Marlene Dietrich. Many accounts come from memoirs, biographies, and later testimony, so the certainty varies by case.", "expert_answer": "John F. Kennedy is reported to have had affairs or relationships with several women, though some claims are disputed. Notable names include:\n\n- **Marilyn Monroe** — actress; widely alleged, not definitively proven.\n- **Judith Campbell Exner** — socialite, who claimed an affair with JFK.\n- **Mimi Alford** — White House intern, who later wrote about their affair.\n- **Mary Pinchot Meyer** — socialite and artist, often reported as a close relationship.\n- **Gunilla von Post** — Swedish aristocrat, who described a romance with JFK.\n- **Inga Arvad** — Danish journalist, linked to Kennedy before his presidency.\n- **Pamela Turnure** — Jacqueline Kennedy’s press secretary, alleged affair.\n- **Marlene Dietrich** — actress, who claimed a brief encounter.\n\nMany accounts come from memoirs, biographies, and later testimony, so the certainty varies by case.", "expert_latency_s": 9.31, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 2071}
{"id": "swebq0119", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.6, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2193, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Semi-presidential system;Republic;Unitary state", "query": "what system of government does guyana have?", "transcript": "What system of government does Guyana have?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Guyana has a **unitary semi-presidential republic** system of government, with an **executive president** serving as both **head of state and head of government**.", "expert_answer": "Guyana has a **unitary semi-presidential republic** system of government, with an **executive president** serving as both **head of state and head of government**.", "expert_latency_s": 1.42, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 831}
