{"id": "swebq0125", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.18, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3145, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "William Penn", "query": "where does name pennsylvania come from?", "transcript": "Where does name Pennsylvania come from?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Pennsylvania comes from the Latin phrase \"Penn's Woods.\" It was named after Admiral Sir William Penn, the father of William Penn, who founded the colony. King Charles II granted the land to William Penn in 1681 and named it Pennsylvania, which is a combination of his name and \"sylvania,\" meaning woods or forests in Latin.", "expert_answer": "Pennsylvania comes from the Latin phrase **“Penn’s Woods.”**\n\nIt was named after **Admiral Sir William Penn**, the father of **William Penn**, who founded the colony. King Charles II granted the land to William Penn in 1681 and named it **Pennsylvania**: **“Penn” + “sylvania”** (Latin for “woodlands” or “forests”).", "expert_latency_s": 2.34, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 1507}
{"id": "swebq0128", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.14, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2285, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Euro", "query": "what kind of money do they use in germany?", "transcript": "What kind of money do they use in Germany?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Germany uses the euro.", "expert_answer": "Germany uses the **euro (€)**.", "expert_latency_s": 0.86, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 149}
{"id": "swebq0131", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.04, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1958, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Mathematician;Physicist;Philosopher;Astronomer;Scientist;Chemist", "query": "who was isaac newton and what did he do?", "transcript": "Who was Isaac Newton and what did he do?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Isaac Newton was an English scientist who changed the way we understand the physical world. He's most famous for his laws of motion and gravity, which explained how things move and why objects attract each other. He also made big advances in math, especially calculus, and studied light to show it’s made of different colors. His work helped start the scientific revolution and is still very important today.", "expert_answer": "Isaac Newton (1642–1727) was an English mathematician, physicist, astronomer, and natural philosopher. He is best known for:\n\n- Formulating the **laws of motion**, which became the foundation of classical mechanics.\n- Developing the **law of universal gravitation**, explaining how objects attract each other, including planets and falling objects.\n- Making major contributions to **calculus**, though Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz developed it independently.\n- Studying **optics**, showing that white light is made up of different colors using a prism.\n- Writing *Philosophiæ Naturalis Principia Mathematica* (1687), one of the most important scientific works ever published.\n\nNewton’s work transformed science and laid the groundwork for much of modern physics and mathematics.", "expert_latency_s": 3.83, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 1885}
{"id": "swebq0134", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 3.95, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2385, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Google Maps;Google Calendar;Google SketchUp;Google Docs and Spreadsheets;Blogger;Picasa;Google Talk;Google X;Gmail", "query": "what products and\\/or services does google offer customers?", "transcript": "What products and or services does Google offer customers?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Google offers a broad range of products and services for consumers, businesses, developers, and advertisers, including search & information tools like Google Search and YouTube; advertising platforms such as Google Ads; productivity software in Gmail, Drive, Docs, and Meet; cloud computing solutions with Google Cloud Platform; mobile operating systems like Android and ChromeOS; web browsers and apps like Chrome and Maps; devices such as Pixel phones and Nest products; payments via Google Pay; developer tools through Firebase and APIs; AI-driven features across its services; education-focused tools like Google Classroom; and business solutions for local listings and marketing.", "expert_answer": "Google offers a broad range of products and services for consumers, businesses, developers, and advertisers, including:\n\n- **Search & information services:** Google Search, Google News, Google Trends\n- **Advertising services:** Google Ads, AdSense, Google Marketing Platform\n- **Productivity & collaboration:** Gmail, Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Calendar, Meet, Google Workspace\n- **Cloud computing:** Google Cloud Platform, cloud storage, databases, analytics, AI/ML tools, cybersecurity services\n- **Mobile & operating systems:** Android, ChromeOS\n- **Web browsers & apps:** Google Chrome, Google Photos, Google Translate, Google Maps, Google Earth\n- **Video & entertainment:** YouTube, YouTube Music, YouTube TV, Google TV\n- **Devices & hardware:** Pixel phones, Pixel Watch, Nest smart-home products, Chromecast/Google TV devices\n- **Payments & shopping:** Google Pay/Google Wallet, Google Shopping\n- **Developer tools:** Firebase, Android Studio, Google APIs\n- **AI products:** Gemini, AI features in Search, Workspace, Cloud AI tools\n- **Education services:** Google Classroom, Workspace for Education\n- **Business listings & local services:** Google Business Profile, Maps advertising\n\nIn short, Google provides search, advertising, software, cloud services, AI tools, mobile platforms, digital content, hardware, and business productivity solutions.", "expert_latency_s": 5.08, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 2848}
{"id": "swebq0137", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 1.48, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1895, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "The Rose That Grew from Concrete", "query": "what book did tupac write?", "transcript": "What book did Tupac write?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Tupac wrote a book of poetry called \"The Rose That Grew from Concrete.\"", "expert_answer": "Tupac Shakur wrote **_The Rose That Grew from Concrete_**, a collection of his poetry.", "expert_latency_s": 3.16, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 431}
{"id": "swebq0140", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.74, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2012, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Jesus Christ;Paul the Apostle;Saint Augustine of Hippo", "query": "what are the beliefs of the roman catholic?", "transcript": "What are the beliefs of the Roman Catholic?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Roman Catholics believe in the teachings of the Catholic Church, centered on things like the Trinity, Jesus Christ as both fully divine and fully human, and salvation through God's grace. They place a lot of importance on the authority of the Church and especially the Pope, as well as the seven sacraments, which are seen as essential for spiritual life. The Eucharist is believed to be the real presence of Christ, not just a symbol. Catholics also honor Mary, the mother of Jesus, and believe in concepts like heaven, hell, and purgatory. Overall, their beliefs combine Scripture, tradition, and the teachings of the Church to guide their faith and practice.", "expert_answer": "Roman Catholics believe in the teachings of the Catholic Church, centered on:\n\n- **One God in the Trinity**: Father, Son, and Holy Spirit.\n- **Jesus Christ**: the Son of God, fully divine and fully human, who died and rose again for humanity’s salvation.\n- **The Bible and Sacred Tradition** as sources of divine revelation.\n- **The authority of the Church**, especially the Pope as the successor of Saint Peter.\n- **The seven sacraments**: Baptism, Eucharist, Confirmation, Reconciliation, Anointing of the Sick, Holy Orders, and Marriage.\n- **The Eucharist** as the real presence of Christ, not merely a symbol.\n- **Salvation by God’s grace**, received through faith, sacraments, and a life of love and good works.\n- **Mary**, the mother of Jesus, as especially honored, and belief in doctrines such as the Immaculate Conception and Assumption.\n- **Communion of saints**, meaning believers can ask saints to pray for them.\n- **Heaven, hell, and purgatory** as part of the afterlife.\n\nIn summary, Roman Catholics follow Christian beliefs as expressed through the Catholic Church, its sacraments, traditions, and teachings.", "expert_latency_s": 6.17, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 3171}
{"id": "swebq0143", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.55, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3041, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince;Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows;Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire;Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone;Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets;Harry Potter and the Order of the Phoenix;Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban", "query": "what are the names of harry potter movies in order?", "transcript": "What are the names of Harry Potter movies in order?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The Harry Potter movies in order are:\\n\\n1. Harry Potter and the Sorcerer’s Stone  \\n2. Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets  \\n3. Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban  \\n4. Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire  \\n5. Harry Potter and the Order of the Phoenix  \\n6. Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince  \\n7. Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 1  \\n8. Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 2", "expert_answer": "The Harry Potter movies in order are:\n\n1. **Harry Potter and the Sorcerer’s Stone** (2001)  \n   *(released as **Harry Potter and the Philosopher’s Stone** in many countries)*  \n2. **Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets** (2002)  \n3. **Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban** (2004)  \n4. **Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire** (2005)  \n5. **Harry Potter and the Order of the Phoenix** (2007)  \n6. **Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince** (2009)  \n7. **Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 1** (2010)  \n8. **Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 2** (2011)", "expert_latency_s": 4.33, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 2796}
{"id": "swebq0146", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.37, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1906, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "The Invasion;Casino Royale;Munich;Enduring Love;Layer Cake;A Kid in King Arthur's Court;The Jacket;The Mother;Sylvia;Road to Perdition", "query": "what films has daniel craig been in?", "transcript": "What films has Daniel Craig been in?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Daniel Craig has appeared in many films, including Casino Royale, Quantum of Solace, Skyfall, Spectre, and No Time to Die as James Bond. He's also known for roles in Knives Out and its sequel, playing detective Benoit Blanc. Other notable films include Layer Cake, Munich, The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo, and Road to Perdition.", "expert_answer": "Daniel Craig has appeared in many films, including:\n\n- **Casino Royale** (2006) — James Bond  \n- **Quantum of Solace** (2008) — James Bond  \n- **Skyfall** (2012) — James Bond  \n- **Spectre** (2015) — James Bond  \n- **No Time to Die** (2021) — James Bond  \n- **Knives Out** (2019) — Benoit Blanc  \n- **Glass Onion: A Knives Out Mystery** (2022) — Benoit Blanc  \n- **Layer Cake** (2004)  \n- **Munich** (2005)  \n- **The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo** (2011)  \n- **Road to Perdition** (2002)  \n- **Defiance** (2008)  \n- **Cowboys & Aliens** (2011)  \n- **Logan Lucky** (2017)  \n- **The Golden Compass** (2007)  \n- **Lara Croft: Tomb Raider** (2001)  \n- **The Mother** (2003)  \n- **Enduring Love** (2004)  \n- **Infamous** (2006)  \n- **Flashbacks of a Fool** (2008)  \n- **Dream House** (2011)  \n- **Kings** (2017)  \n- **Queer** (2024)\n\nHe is best known for playing **James Bond** and later detective **Benoit Blanc** in the *Knives Out* films.", "expert_latency_s": 8.49, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 1734}
