{"id": "swebq0179", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 1.81, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2255, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "2012", "query": "when will the world end mayans?", "transcript": "When will the world end Mayans?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The Mayans didn't actually predict the world would end. The big date, December 21, 2012, was just the end of a calendar cycle for them, kind of like flipping to a new page in their book—not an apocalypse. So there's no specific Mayan date that says the world will end.", "expert_answer": "The Mayans did **not** predict the world would end.\n\nThe claim came from the end of a cycle in the Maya Long Count calendar on **December 21, 2012**. For the Maya, this was like a calendar “reset” or the start of a new cycle—not an apocalypse. So there is **no Mayan date for the end of the world**.", "expert_latency_s": 3.59, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 1569}
